  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Substance $A$ (initially 30 g) evaporates at a rate of $1\\frac12$ g per minute while substance $B$ (initially 20 g) evaporates at a rate of $\\frac23$ g per minute. $y_A$ and $y_B$ grams are the amounts of substances $A$ and $B$ respectively at time $t$ minutes after the substances begin to evaporate.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Write down formulas for $y_A$ and $y_B$ in terms of $t$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y_A=30-\\frac32t$, $y_B=20-\\frac23t$.",
          "worked": "Amount remaining = initial amount − rate × time.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y_A&=30-\\frac32t\\\\y_B&=20-\\frac23t\\end{align*}$$\n\nThese rules apply until each substance reaches 0 g: $0\\le t\\le20$ for $A$ and $0\\le t\\le30$ for $B$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the time it takes for substance $A$ to evaporate to 0 g.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "20 minutes.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}30-\\frac32t&=0\\\\\\frac32t&=30\\\\t&=30\\times\\frac23\\\\t&=20\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstance $A$ reaches 0 g after 20 minutes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "After how long do both substances have the same weight?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "12 minutes.",
          "worked": "Set the two amounts equal.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}30-\\frac32t&=20-\\frac23t\\\\10&=\\left(\\frac32-\\frac23\\right)t\\\\10&=\\frac56t\\\\t&=12\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck in both rules:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y_A&=30-\\frac32(12)\\\\y_A&=12\\text{ g}\\\\y_B&=20-\\frac23(12)\\\\y_B&=12\\text{ g}\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth substances weigh 12 g after 12 minutes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": {
