        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y_A=a-bt$, $y_B=c-dt$.",
          "worked": "Subtract the amount lost in $t$ minutes from each initial amount.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y_A&=a-bt\\\\y_B&=c-dt\\end{align*}$$\n\nEach rule applies while that substance remains.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q8-e",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Find in terms of $a$, $b$, $c$ and $d$:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p17-q8-e-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "the time when substance $A$ and $B$ are of the same weight",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$t=\\dfrac{c-a}{d-b}$ minutes, provided $d\\ne b$ and the time lies in the physical range of both models.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a-bt&=c-dt\\\\(d-b)t&=c-a\\\\t&=\\frac{c-a}{d-b}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis gives the time in minutes when $d\\ne b$, provided $t\\ge0$ and neither model gives a negative amount. If $d=b$, the amounts are equal throughout their common model interval when $a=c$; otherwise they do not meet within that interval.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 30
          },
          {
            "id": "p17-q8-e-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "the weight of each substance $A$ and $B$ when they are of the same weight, expressing your answer as a fraction.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{ad-bc}{d-b}$ g each, under the conditions in part e(i).\n\nSubstitute the common time into either amount rule.",
              "worked": "Substitute $t=\\frac{c-a}{d-b}$ into $y_A=a-bt$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y_A&=a-b\\left(\\frac{c-a}{d-b}\\right)\\\\y_A&=\\frac{a(d-b)-b(c-a)}{d-b}\\\\y_A&=\\frac{ad-ab-bc+ab}{d-b}\\\\y_A&=\\frac{ad-bc}{d-b}\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck using the other rule:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y_B&=c-d\\left(\\frac{c-a}{d-b}\\right)\\\\y_B&=\\frac{c(d-b)-d(c-a)}{d-b}\\\\y_B&=\\frac{ad-bc}{d-b}\\end{align*}$$\n\nEach substance weighs $\\frac{ad-bc}{d-b}$ g, provided the conditions in part e(i) hold.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 34
          }
        ]
      }
